# Generated artifacts whose exact bytes are the contract. The canonical
# serializer (engine/serialize/canonical.ts) defines them: keys sorted by
# UTF-16 code unit, every array expanded one item per line, LF, one trailing
# newline. Prettier collapses short arrays onto one line — different bytes,
# and therefore a replay that no longer matches its recording.
#
# The two agreed by accident until a recording first contained a non-empty
# array. Whichever tool writes a file owns its formatting; regenerate these
# with `npm run fixtures:update` and `npm run schema:update`.
